{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded","id":153881,"title":"Independent Dragon Blooded?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-30T08:54:43-07:00","id":153881,"title":"Independent Dragon Blooded?","content":"I've only read the core book, and find the Dragon Blooded more interesting than the solar. I have a question about the Dragon Blooded. Are there independent Dragon Blooded who do not belong to the realm? As an example Dragon Blood mercenaries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3151-grey-knight","name":"Grey Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T09:04:59-07:00","id":153911,"title":"","content":"Oh sure, they're all over the place. That's one of the advantages of passing your power down through blood; almost everyone in Creation has at least a few traces of dragonblood heritage in them, so dragons can appear anywhere in Creation and the Realm often doesn't find them until they've decided they have better things to do than serving the empire. Those kinds of dragons are typically called outcastes or &quot;lost eggs.&quot; There's a chapter or two dedicated to them in the Dragon-Blooded splatbook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":834,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","user":"HK-87","date":". 05-30-2014, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T09:09:19-07:00","id":153917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grey Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded#post153881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've only read the core book, and find the Dragon Blooded more interesting than the solar. I have a question about the Dragon Blooded. Are there independent Dragon Blooded who do not belong to the realm? As an example Dragon Blood mercenaries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in terms of non-Realm DBs, they basically split into two groups.<br /> <br /> The first is the Seventh Legion of Lookshy, which is the largest enclave of Dragon-Blooded (and the largest stockpile of First Age tech) outside of the Realm. They follow a very militaristic approach, modeling themselves after the Shogunate, and are separated primarily into five &quot;Gens.&quot; They're relatively nice, at least compared to the Realm, but they still exercise their Exalted muscle to keep their neighbors in line. As a result, all Dragon-Blooded of Lookshy are trained to be soldiers, and must complete a mandatory military service. You can find more info on Lookshy from the Compass of Terrestrial Directions: The Scavenger Lands.<br /> <br /> The second group is the &quot;Lost Eggs,&quot; the collective name for any Dragon-Blooded born outside of a Great House or Gens. Although certain Houses (and many of the Gens) pursue Lost Eggs to add to their weakened bloodlines, prospects for Lost Eggs tend to be pretty slim- those that are adopted by the Realm must either join the military or the Immaculate Order, and any attempt to establish a power base outside of the Realm of Lookshy will generally attract the attention of the Wyld Hunt. That said, Dragon-Blooded are still Exalted, and a few have managed to thrive in spite of everything they have going against them. You can find more info about Lost Eggs from the Manual of Exalted Power: The Dragon-Blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;We do not quit playing because we grow old, we grow old because we quit playing.&quot; - Oliver Wendell Holmes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","name":"MrInsecure","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T09:17:34-07:00","id":153929,"title":"","content":"You can be a strong independent Outcaste who don't need no Great House!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T09:43:57-07:00","id":153949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrInsecure</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=153917#post153917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The second group is the &quot;Lost Eggs,&quot; the collective name for any Dragon-Blooded born outside of a Great House or Gens. Although certain Houses (and many of the Gens) pursue Lost Eggs to add to their weakened bloodlines, prospects for Lost Eggs tend to be pretty slim- those that are adopted by the Realm must either join the military or the Immaculate Order, and any attempt to establish a power base outside of the Realm of Lookshy will generally attract the attention of the Wyld Hunt. That said, Dragon-Blooded are still Exalted, and a few have managed to thrive in spite of everything they have going against them. You can find more info about Lost Eggs from the Manual of Exalted Power: The Dragon-Blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>...what?<br /> <br /> That's completely off-base.<br /> <br /> The Wyld Hunt deals with the Anathema and existential threats such as the Fair Folk; they don't have anything to do with the Outcaste. Sure, Outcastes/Lost Eggs can get in trouble with the Realm, but dealing with them will never be a job for the Wyld Hunt - only for Dynasts or the Legions. And since there are more Outcastes than there are Dynasts, conducting a policy of systematically rooting out Lost Eggs that cause trouble would be a very poor idea indeed.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, Outcastes thrive outside the Realm. The majority of nations or organization with influence have Outcastes in their employ, from Halta to the Haslanti League to the Lintha, with others working for the Guild or just becoming rulers in their own right. The Outcastes have incredible assets, and life is much, much easier from the get-go for them than it is for a mortal - those who want to strike out on their own might have a tough time doing so as would anyone, but the world at large prizes and desires their talents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T12:00:14-07:00","id":154074,"title":"","content":"Yes, given the nature of the Dragon Blooded, I'd say the main thing they have going against them as that they're not much stronger than everything else around them, in contrast to Celestial Exalted. Even for those who have means and ambition and decent amount of luck in order to reign over something, their comparatively short lifespans might make their achievements feel limited as compared to those other Exalted, or even the Realm.<br /> <br /> Even Lookshy derives a lot of its power from having a large number of Exalted, and reliable means to keep producing them; there are a fair number of Outcastes throughout the world, but the majority are on their own* and their bloodlines aren't likely to reliably produce Exalted descendents.<br /> <br /> I'd say most are only pressured by the Realm, at worst, unless they show a directly disruptive attitude. It's not as if they're a major threat to the status quo, nor is the Realm particularly opposed to the idea of Terrestrial Exalted ruling things.<br /> <br /> * I'd also say that the majority of such groupings are formed as attempts at impromptu Wyld Hunts. Maybe the ones that survive bond in a way that holds them together, but that's at least two counts of a fairly big maybe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T13:08:19-07:00","id":154124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=154074#post154074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even for those who have means and ambition and decent amount of luck in order to reign over something, their comparatively short lifespans might make their achievements feel limited as compared to those other Exalted, or even the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that the average PC is allowed to have great achievements in the span of a campaign, I don't think the fact that DB live &quot;only&quot; a couple centuries matters much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T13:29:58-07:00","id":154144,"title":"","content":"Generally, Dragon-Blooded out from under the guidance of the Realm or Lookshy usually do pretty well for themselves. They have abilities far beyond the average mortal, even without dedicated training. It isn't hard for them to achieve positions of authority, power, and wealth (relative to their civilization, anyway). They will take over small groups, like a nomadic group of 20 pretty much right away. Groups of 50-100 after some training and experience. Larger groups of 10,000+, they will usually pick up a position of authority, such as head of a merchant company or local guild affiliate, royal counselor, captain of the royal guard, or some other position with some training and experience, and they likely won't be the only Dragon-Blooded around. They probably won't become a local King unless they put a great deal of effort into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T13:39:56-07:00","id":154153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=154124#post154124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given that the average PC is allowed to have great achievements in the span of a campaign, I don't think the fact that DB live &quot;only&quot; a couple centuries matters much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Characters in the setting backstory are not PCs, disregarding alternate history Shards.<br /> <br /> More than that, the fact that they don't live for longer than the Realm has been around is to make a point about how, whatever their achievements, they're long dead, and most lack the recourse to have achievements last longer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T14:03:05-07:00","id":154168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=154153#post154153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Characters in the setting backstory are not PCs, disregarding alternate history Shards.<br /> <br /> More than that, the fact that they don't live for longer than the Realm has been around is to make a point about how, whatever their achievements, they're long dead, and most lack the recourse to have achievements last longer.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is nice to have extension options at least, for those players who are bothered by the idea of being shorter lived. Taking a gem of Immortality or some Resistance charms can extend the lifespans of the ambitious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2394-grifnir","name":"Grifnir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T15:47:32-07:00","id":154239,"title":"","content":"There are some rather appealing options for Dragon-Bloods outside the Realm and Lookshy.<br /> <br /> Cherak are the Realm's uncouth Northern neighbours, where poor weather and hard living have forced grim austerity on the people and the leaders plot incompetently against the decadent Southerners. It's basically Scotland.<br /> <br /> The Grass Spiders are an order of fanatical Eastern assassins trained in esoteric techniques. They also have a good sense of humour, which I suppose is nice as far as these things go.<br /> <br /> The Five Shade Association are a confederation of old Shogunate crime families that wage a guerilla war against the Realm with large networks of enlightened and elemental agents and their thoroughly silly martial arts.<br /> <br /> My favourite Outcaste group though, is a non canon one. In the closing days of the old forum, Dean Shomshak gave us the <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/defaultb0d0.html?g=posts&amp;t=83679\" target=\"_blank\">Ollantijaya</a>, who I thoroughly intend to use at some point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T15:49:42-07:00","id":154240,"title":"","content":"Personally, I imagine that most minor nations are actually ruled by the Dragonblooded. Those who aren't born into minor dynasties likely end up as D&amp;D style wandering adventurers, ganging together in impromptu Circles, building fame and fortune while honing their skills. Once they've had their fill of adventure, they settle down - doing whatever they feel like, most likely involving at least one spouse and a few kids. If they are at all ambitious, they will either founding a kingdom of their own, or taking over a preexisting one. And for the King, marrying off his son or daughter to an ambitious Dragonblood is a good way to secure the future of their kingdom and their bloodline - and possibly adding the favour of the Dragons while they're at it. No matter the particulars of the dispute, Dragonblooded rulers will almost always triumph over un-Exalted rulers, and thus become the dominant parties in their regions.<br /> <br /> I can imagine that Godbloods work similarly; they are to Terrestrials as Terrestrials are to Celestials. Lacking native Charms, they are probably more inclined to focus on the paths of power available to them; Martial Arts and Sorcery, thus becoming the wizards in the towers, the witches in the marshes, the monks in the temples, and the Captains of the local Templar Order - Golden Janissaries anyone?<br /> <br /> This ties in neatly with the idea that Lunars are more or less behind every nation ruled by mortals, because otherwise mortal rule doesn't make much sense. I mean, in a barbarian society, the guy who can single-handedly kill a hundred men is the undisputed king; in an aristocratic society, the bloodlines which demonstrably possess actual power will rule; and in a democracy, the guy who is inhumanly persuasive is going to win every election.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Aretii: &quot;As one of the players described it, 'After initiation, it was actually a relief seeing who had eyepatches or bandaged hands - you know what <i>they</i> sacrificed, instead of wondering what bits people cut out of their own souls to gain power.'&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/578-lord-sia","name":"Lord Sia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T17:14:18-07:00","id":154306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Sia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=154240#post154240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I imagine that most minor nations are actually ruled by the Dragonblooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pfft.<br /> <br /> Okay, one, I wouldn't call most of the splotches on the map &quot;nations.&quot; Most of them have barely advanced beyond the city-state; folks who live two hundred miles away from each other are not going to consider each other as part of the same culture, even if a guy with a crown places his boots on both their necks.<br /> <br /> This is also something that the <i>300</i> movie and its recent sequel <i>keep</i> getting wrong. <b>There was no &quot;Greece.&quot;</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Sia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=154240#post154240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those who aren't born into minor dynasties likely end up as D&amp;D style wandering adventurers, ganging together in impromptu Circles, building fame and fortune while honing their skills. Once they've had their fill of adventure, they settle down - doing whatever they feel like, most likely involving at least one spouse and a few kids. If they are at all ambitious, they will either founding a kingdom of their own, or taking over a preexisting one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or dying in the attempt. Or joining the Guild. Or forming a clan of ninjas. Or taking up sorcery. Or going over to the Realm. Or finding a place in Heaven. Or descending into Malfeas seeking glory and wealth there, never to be seen again. Or founding an incestuous family in the desert while searching the sands for immortality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Sia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=154240#post154240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No matter the particulars of the dispute, Dragonblooded rulers will almost always triumph over un-Exalted rulers, and thus become the dominant parties in their regions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yawn. Okay, I'm done with this conversation. Can't take you seriously at this point anymore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Sia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=154240#post154240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This ties in neatly with the idea that Lunars are more or less behind every nation ruled by mortals, because otherwise mortal rule doesn't make much sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>said</i> I'm done with this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T17:49:53-07:00","id":154390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=154153#post154153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Characters in the setting backstory are not PCs, disregarding alternate history Shards.<br /> <br /> More than that, the fact that they don't live for longer than the Realm has been around is to make a point about how, whatever their achievements, they're long dead, and most lack the recourse to have achievements last longer.</div> </div> </div> </div>That said, with anagathics and other stuff it ain't much of a stretch for a careful and successful DB, dynast or not, to live 400-500 years. So, yeah, you probably won't live enough to make works to surpass the Realm but you might live enough to set up the aristocratic household/independent dynasty/splinter gens that will. The Realm has 11 dynastic houses - an equal number of houses sprang up and disappeared in its more than 7 centuries of history, who's to say some lone but enterprising outcaste won't be the next Ragara, Manosque Viridian, Mnemon, Bagresh K\u00f6l, Perfect or who knows who else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T18:09:51-07:00","id":154404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Sia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=154240#post154240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No matter the particulars of the dispute, Dragonblooded rulers will almost always triumph over un-Exalted rulers, and thus become the dominant parties in their regions.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> This ties in neatly with the idea that Lunars are more or less behind every nation ruled by mortals, because otherwise mortal rule doesn't make much sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, Dragonblooded rulers will almost always triumph over un-Exalted rulers in a straight contest. That does not equate to them ruling everybody because a; straight contests are for suckers and b; Creation is <i>fucking huge</i>.<br /> <br /> And no, Lunars are not &quot;more or less behind&quot; every nation ruled by mortals. The Thousand Streams River is one of the most dumbassed things to come out of how 2e handled Lunars, and lemme tell you, <i>that there is some stiff competition.</i><br /> <br /> You know who's secretly behind most mortal nations in Creation? Mortals. Competent, entrenched mortal regimes who are unlikely to ever encounter one of the Chosen. Those that do will remain sovereign powers because they've had decades or centuries to solidify their power base, while a wandering Dragonblood is one dude with a fancy sword.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are no problems, only plothooks.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P2AuLM6D1Et9mWQVJp-ugWujFJhTi2VwQBtOazOW1Mg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Terrifying Argent Witches Hub</a><br /> <i>Originally posted by </i><b><i>Dex Davican</i></b><br /> I need them for my collection: <i>Enormous Gonads of 2012: A Retrospective.</i>","edited":{"userid":920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","user":"Imrix","date":". 05-30-2014, 09:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","name":"Imrix","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T18:33:07-07:00","id":154415,"title":"","content":"I always found it disappointing that as good as the Aspect books of 1E were, they only covered Realm Dragonbloods. I want to hear about Lost Eggs, or Outcasts. I want bloodlines of Dragonblooded significant to cultures, nations, or even religions.<br /> <br /> This also tied into that neat idea that the chances of Dragonblooded children increased by having elemental blood in your line, and that this was further construed in primitive cultures into families of mortals and Elementals, where Dragonblooded are understood to come from Elementals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T19:34:15-07:00","id":154457,"title":"","content":"Funnily enough I usually run it exactly the opposite. DBs are very seldom the rulers, usually they're integrated into kingdoms in different ways.<br /> <br /> Basically the way I look at is is this, Dragonblooded are not particularly better at ruling than mortals. The magic gives them a slight edge in some situations and discounting excellencies those situations are somewhat rare. On the other hand Dragonblooded are hella good soldiers, they even have magic that specifically gets better if they're not the ones giving the orders. It so much better to have a DB go around breaking bandits in half than to have them sit on a throne delegating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T20:42:45-07:00","id":154495,"title":"","content":"The Outcaste are basically the best thing in Exalted (besides Alchemicals, toward whom I carry an uncommon bias). I've played several and never regretted it.<br /> <br /> The Realm and Lookshy carry a fair amount of baggage with them, being soldiers or sorcerer-engineers or aristocrats but generally having a structure to build their live around. (And, to their tremendous advantage, other Dragon-Bloods to back them up.)<br /> <br /> The Outcaste can do absolutely, positively <i>anything</i> they want on a level that even Solars can't manage. I play one who is a paladin. I played another who was a farmer, because that's what he wanted to do. (Speed Farmer irrigates Cecelyne, saves the world.) Yet another who was from a long-standing river trader family (with DBs of their own besides her) that were rivals to the Guild. They are dragon-blooded freed of the soldiery and aristocratic trappings, who have the whole world available to them. And though they can be the greatest allies to your Solars, they are also liable to be the fiercest opponents to a return to days of old because they are chefs and chieftans, warriors and wanderers, matrons and madmen and masons, assassins and artists and accountants and you will <i>never</i> get them to go back to being soldiers.<br /> <br /> *cough*<br /> <br /> So, er, yeah. Independent Dragon-Bloods are everywhere, doing everything, and they are awesome and I hope to <i>Burning Feather</i> that Ex3e gives us them in all their glory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","user":"Guancyto","date":". 05-31-2014, 12:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T22:01:58-07:00","id":154519,"title":"","content":"I really hope the Outcast character creation doesn't suck so much in EX3, I know they don't have the same resources as DB from Lookshy or the Realm, but it still fells kinda shitty when you stat up a Outcaste with a cool story but you don't get the same tools to make him as the other DB at the table...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T22:18:20-07:00","id":154525,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, I should note that almost every game I've been in that has included Outcastes in any meaningful way has either been entirely Outcastes or has given them a better start than the books do (and, in fact, when I see a nice revised chargen my first reaction is &quot;finally, time to play an Outcaste!&quot;). Otherwise said 'outcastes' will inevitably be fully-built exiles from the Realm just for the <i>huge</i> disparity in stats.<br /> <br /> Obviously it's not such a big deal if they're just your allies or lieutenants or super secret assassin contacts.<br /> <br /> Fake edit: And nobody has mentioned Forest Witches! They're totally a thing (but somebody else can probably do the exposition on them better)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T23:17:06-07:00","id":154590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guancyto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=154525#post154525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fake edit: And nobody has mentioned Forest Witches! They're totally a thing (but somebody else can probably do the exposition on them better)</div> </div> </div> </div>I forgot about those guys!<br /> <br /> They sure are... a thing. <br /> <br /> Honestly I've never been able to pin down what their deal is. They are sorcerers or something who collect artifacts to sustain some creepy magic parallel dimension, but they are also ghosts, but not really, and some of them are horrifying mutant people.<br /> <br /> They're a refreshing change, to be sure, but they seem to require more attention than I am able to give them.<br /> <br /> Oh, and there's also Eos and Ossissa, a large organization of wyld-sailing dragon pirates who spend all their time dicking with the Guild and the Lintha.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T23:56:28-07:00","id":154596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=154415#post154415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always found it disappointing that as good as the Aspect books of 1E were, they only covered Realm Dragonbloods. I want to hear about Lost Eggs, or Outcasts. I want bloodlines of Dragonblooded significant to cultures, nations, or even religions.<br /> <br /> This also tied into that neat idea that the chances of Dragonblooded children increased by having elemental blood in your line, and that this was further construed in primitive cultures into families of mortals and Elementals, where Dragonblooded are understood to come from Elementals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mm. Looking at the Aspect books, the majority of sig characters (21) were Realm DBs. Two were outcaste brought in (one into the Order, the other into the legions), and two were outcaste who remained independent. The balance towards the outcaste could have been better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T03:15:25-07:00","id":154639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=154306#post154306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, one, I wouldn't call most of the splotches on the map &quot;nations.&quot; Most of them have barely advanced beyond the city-state; folks who live two hundred miles away from each other are not going to consider each other as part of the same culture, even if a guy with a crown places his boots on both their necks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and? I'm using &quot;king&quot; in the meaning &quot;sovereign ruler&quot;, with no qualifier on how large an area he must rule. Besides, say that a Dragonblood claims everything within an day's ride of his home, that's almost three thousand square miles. Call it thirty people per square mile - not particularly dense at all - and that's almost a hundred thousand people in his domain. I'd call that a kingdom. Maybe the Dragonblood puts his boot on everyone's neck, in which case they call him &quot;Lord&quot; lest he kills them - or he doesn't, and they call him &quot;Lord&quot; because whenever there's trouble, he's the one they turn to.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or dying in the attempt. Or joining the Guild. Or forming a clan of ninjas. Or taking up sorcery. Or going over to the Realm. Or finding a place in Heaven. Or descending into Malfeas seeking glory and wealth there, never to be seen again. Or founding an incestuous family in the desert while searching the sands for immortality. </div> </div> </div>Yep, there are <i>tons </i>of things a Lost Egg can do. However, you'll not that anything involving risk is significantly more likely to result in death, while those who settle down and raise families - no matter where or how - are considerably more likely to end up producing new Exalts. Over time, this favours the creation of small Dynasties here and there; merchant dynasties, hidden ninja villages, sorcerous traditions, nomadic clans... And any and all of them are going to have a disproportionate amount of power and influence because of their Dragonblooded leaders.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yawn. Okay, I'm done with this conversation. Can't take you seriously at this point anymore.<br /> <br /> I <i>said</i> I'm done with this. </div> </div> </div>... Yeah, that came off as &quot;Only The Exalted Matter&quot;, didn't it? I apologise for that; however, while being Exalted is not an &quot;I Win&quot; button, it is a massive advantage. This, you can't deny. And when the world is made up of shattered and divided land, filled with roaming monsters and forgotten secrets, natural selection favours the guy who can throw fireballs with his mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imrix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=154404#post154404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, Dragonblooded rulers will almost always triumph over un-Exalted rulers in a straight contest. That does not equate to them ruling everybody because a; straight contests are for suckers and b; Creation is <i>fucking huge</i>.<br /> <br /> And no, Lunars are not &quot;more or less behind&quot; every nation ruled by mortals. The Thousand Streams River is one of the most dumbassed things to come out of how 2e handled Lunars, and lemme tell you, <i>that there is some stiff competition.</i><br /> <br /> You know who's secretly behind most mortal nations in Creation? Mortals. Competent, entrenched mortal regimes who are unlikely to ever encounter one of the Chosen. Those that do will remain sovereign powers because they've had decades or centuries to solidify their power base, while a wandering Dragonblood is one dude with a fancy sword.</div> </div> </div> </div>See the above. And true, straight contests are for suckers, but all else being equal, the Exalted win something like nine times out of ten. Yes, Creation is Huge; it's one of the reasons we love it, because you can fit pretty much anything you want into it somewhere.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I'm not really happy with TSR either, although it may sound like it. Mostly because it makes no fucking sense that they'd all be in on this. I can see a faction doing it, spearheaded by an Elder or two, but all of them? No.<br /> <br /> Yes, sheer numbers do mean that most nations are run by mortals. Sheer power means that the Dragonblooded that are part of these societies possess a disproportionate amount of influence - even if they do not sit on the throne, they doubtlessly have the throne's ear. IIRC, the Realm has about half of the world's population of DBs; call it ten thousand as a lower limit, which means that the world has a total DB population of about twenty thousand - I'd personally bet on at least five times that number though. Lookshy has another thousand, maybe two, and let's say that another two or three thousand are spread between Heaven and Hell. That leaves at least five thousand DBs at large in the world, doing all of things everyone here has already mentioned.<br /> <br /> To drag in a real-world comparison; the top 1% wealthy people may not directly rule the world, but they do possess a major influence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Aretii: &quot;As one of the players described it, 'After initiation, it was actually a relief seeing who had eyepatches or bandaged hands - you know what <i>they</i> sacrificed, instead of wondering what bits people cut out of their own souls to gain power.'&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/578-lord-sia","name":"Lord Sia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T04:31:59-07:00","id":154693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Sia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=154639#post154639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To drag in a real-world comparison; the top 1% wealthy people may not directly rule the world, but they do possess a major influence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... that happened.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Masters of Jade</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bTo that end, money becomes a form of Exaltation.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T04:59:33-07:00","id":154704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Sia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=154639#post154639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes, sheer numbers do mean that most nations are run by mortals. Sheer power means that the Dragonblooded that are part of these societies possess a disproportionate amount of influence - even if they do not sit on the throne, they doubtlessly have the throne's ear.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd doubt it, on grounds ranging from &quot;a lot of rulers won't want to let a Terrestrial anywhere near them&quot; to &quot;a lot of Terrestrials won't care&quot;.<br /> <br /> They're not like, say, the Zenith Caste Solars, selected from amongst those who already have an inclination towards ruling people. To the extent that there's a selection criteria for the Dragon Blooded at all (and I'd say there's not much), I perceive it as the kind of thing that often points in entirely different directions than ruling over people. Even if it didn't, unless you already have a knack and a desire for it, I'd imagine that most don't especially care to use their power to reign over others because that's such a hassle; people always expecting you to solve their problems or arbitrate their disputes.<br /> <br /> Why bother yourself with it in your talents and proclivities are more towards scholarly pursuit, architectural development, honing and proving sword skills, finding adventure on the open seas, going around fixing the wounded and diseased?<br /> <br /> These are, of course, by no means all that the Dragon Blooded can do, or that all of them want to do or such; they're not elementally fixated or something, they're still human beings.<br /> <br /> But they're things a person can want that have nothing to do with ruling folks.<br /> <br /> The desire to rule the lives of others is not the natural inclination of everybody, or even of all powerful people. If anything, it's kind of a minority thing.<br /> <br /> Why bother to rule them, or influence the ones who die, when you've got power enough to pursue your actual dreams?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Sia</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That leaves at least five thousand DBs at large in the world, doing all of things everyone here has already mentioned.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a drop in the ocean.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Sia</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">To drag in a real-world comparison; the top 1% wealthy people may not directly rule the world, but they do possess a major influence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wealthy people possess a considerable influence only because they want and have the means to bend government towards the purpose of safeguarding their wealth. At least a significant amount of the time; it's not a one hundred percent thing that people leverage wealth in order to push their ideologies.<br /> <br /> When you're Exalted, you might be powerful in a way that securing your wealth or other desires isn't necessarily something government can stand in the way of.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T07:09:46-07:00","id":154796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=154704#post154704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip</div> </div> </div> </div>Good points, and plenty of food for thought. Guess I'm a bit too locked in the idea of a romanticised nobility... Annoying. Excuse me while I fixate on Soviet Autochtonia for a while; that ought to rid me of such silly notions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Aretii: &quot;As one of the players described it, 'After initiation, it was actually a relief seeing who had eyepatches or bandaged hands - you know what <i>they</i> sacrificed, instead of wondering what bits people cut out of their own souls to gain power.'&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/578-lord-sia","name":"Lord Sia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T07:30:31-07:00","id":154815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=154704#post154704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're not like, say, the Zenith Caste Solars, selected from amongst those who already have an inclination towards ruling people. To the extent that there's a selection criteria for the Dragon Blooded at all (and I'd say there's not much), I perceive it as the kind of thing that often points in entirely different directions than ruling over people. Even if it didn't, unless you already have a knack and a desire for it, I'd imagine that most don't especially care to use their power to reign over others because that's such a hassle; people always expecting you to solve their problems or arbitrate their disputes.<br /> <br /> Why bother yourself with it in your talents and proclivities are more towards scholarly pursuit, architectural development, honing and proving sword skills, finding adventure on the open seas, going around fixing the wounded and diseased?<br /> <br /> These are, of course, by no means all that the Dragon Blooded can do, or that all of them want to do or such; they're not elementally fixated or something, they're still human beings.<br /> <br /> But they're things a person can want that have nothing to do with ruling folks.<br /> <br /> The desire to rule the lives of others is not the natural inclination of everybody, or even of all powerful people. If anything, it's kind of a minority thing.<br /> <br /> Why bother to rule them, or influence the ones who die, when you've got power enough to pursue your actual dreams?</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, the Realm has spent a great deal of time and effort educating everyone that it has any influence over that the Dragon-Blooded are the ordained rulers of Creation and anything that they want is theirs by right. That's not a trivial influence over the Dragon-Blooded themselves or the people they would seek to rule.<br /> <br /> Zeniths are priest-king royalty, true... but the Dragon Blooded are still the nobility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T08:26:48-07:00","id":154844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imrix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=154404#post154404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, Dragonblooded rulers will almost always triumph over un-Exalted rulers in a straight contest. That does not equate to them ruling everybody because a; straight contests are for suckers and b; Creation is <i>fucking huge</i>. And no, Lunars are not &amp;quot;more or less behind&amp;quot; every nation ruled by mortals. The Thousand Streams River is one of the most dumbassed things to come out of how 2e handled Lunars, and lemme tell you, <i>that there is some stiff competition.</i> You know who's secretly behind most mortal nations in Creation? Mortals. Competent, entrenched mortal regimes who are unlikely to ever encounter one of the Chosen. Those that do will remain sovereign powers because they've had decades or centuries to solidify their power base, while a wandering Dragonblood is one dude with a fancy sword.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually i would think the Sidereals would be behind most mortal nations in creation because i would think any nations ruler who displeased the siddys would have a very unfortunate destiny. I do think it makes sense that dragonblooded rulers would trump mortal rulers in most cases, but outside the realm and lookshy, dragonbloods are rare....about 1 in 10000 or so, right? and many of them who dont want to attract the attention of the realm will be keeping a very low profile. As do Lunars who decide they want to live anywhere in the threshold. no exalt wants to attract the attention of the wyld hunt. thats not a recipe for a long and fruitful life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T12:19:06-07:00","id":155094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=154815#post154815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Zeniths are priest-king royalty, true... but the Dragon Blooded are still the nobility.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love that the Dragon Blooded contain factors that incline them towards aristocratic social organisation and family planning priorities, but I'd also think that there were a lot of complicated and extended social and historical factors that went into them actual crystallizing these imperatives into <i>being</i> a collection of aristocratic families, only truly realised in the body of the Scarlet Dynasty (which is to say, daimyos or no daimyos, even the Shogunate hadn't fully gotten into it).<br /> <br /> I imagine many places and long periods of the First Age in which the Celestial Exalted, and more than a few of the actual Terrestrials themselves, were irritated by how many of those Exalted took their hereditary nature as cause to band together, become insular and style themselves as a kind of aristocracy. I see many Terrestrials who didn't really care to base their own power on how many of their children they could get to Exalt (or at least placed higher priority on marrying into other powerful social groups, securing their own position with the promise of having members of their own people Exalt throughout the generations), who break away from highly traditionalist core family groups and thus have lower Breeding (and introducing bloodlines that persist in such).<br /> <br /> And yet, they're still Exalted, they still have all the powers necessary to function as scholar-soldier-sodalt-bureaucrats of the highest order, and the sprawling Realm and all of its greatest heroes ready to make use of their talents, with ready institutions to scoop them up, bring them together and find work for them.<br /> <br /> If there are as many Dragon Blooded outside of the Realm of the Age of Sorrows as there are within it, then that would seem to suggest you can get decent numbers at large without needing to buy very much into letting them act like an aristocracy, nor treat them as such. Good breeding only matters if you want to make sure that any given dozen Exalts are <i>your</i> children (or grandchildren or so on), and thus nominally have power over them, and that kind of... provincialism only really confers significant power in a time like the Age of Sorrows.<br /> <br /> That's if you keep the numbers as they currently are; before the contagion, they might have been ten times greater, or a hundred. When there are hundreds of thousands of other Terrestrial Exalted are out there in the wider world (and there's an actual sense of connectivity to <i>make</i> there be a wider world), what does it matter if only one of your children inherits the power?<br /> <br /> I see the mid-to-late First Age as a time in which the overwhelming trend of society for the Terrestrial Exalted was more like those animes where you've got mystical people in modern Japan who are all clannish and still acting as though their aristocratic sensibilities are relevant, and you've got the young rebel who wants to go out and be master of their own destiny. Except where the rebels are the majority, the mystical clans are known to society at large, and the greater trend setters give a lot more support to the rebels (even if the insular traditionalists are conferred with a degree of respect and protection, in honour of their services and those of their ancestors). The time when the stronger trend towards banding together in a way that makes family bonds more pronounced and valued is about the time in which they call themselves Dragon Blooded more than Terrestrial Exalted (in other words, when they start agitating for Usurpation).<br /> <br /> So what I'm getting at is... Dragon Blooded are only really nobility when they want to present themselves as such, and <i>that</i> only really comes from the ones who <b>are</b> interested in rule (because it certainly helps to firmly establish your reign when you're being aided by a dozen or so deferential Exalts). The Scarlet Dynasty is the logical conclusion of Terrestrial Exalted who want to rule things, and even <i>they</i> have people who just don't buy into being socialized to want to rule, and go off into the morass of alternate ambitions found amongst the scattered, disorganized Dragon Blooded of the Threshold.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, the Realm has spent a great deal of time and effort educating everyone that it has any influence over that the Dragon-Blooded are the ordained rulers of Creation and anything that they want is theirs by right. That's not a trivial influence over the Dragon-Blooded themselves or the people they would seek to rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>One is in a bit of a Catch-22 there; any place where the Scarlet Dynasty has such a powerful conditioning influence is a place where Outcastes will have little recourse to reign over people, and any place that would be more open to Outcastes is a place that has likely been a bit resistant to (or distant from) Realm indoctrination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 05-31-2014, 03:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T12:20:16-07:00","id":155096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NuSoardGraphite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=154844#post154844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Actually i would think the Sidereals would be behind most mortal nations in creation because i would think any nations ruler who displeased the siddys would have a very unfortunate destiny.</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt the Sidereals have the interest to micromanage the destiny of powerful people in Creation, and they certainly don't have the resources.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T12:46:55-07:00","id":155110,"title":"","content":"Actually, I think a more succinct summary of my prior point is: the hereditary nature of the Terrestrial Exaltation does lend itself to aristocratic drama narratives, especially when it intersects with those Dragon Blooded who have wanted to hold authoritative power (which just so happens to be the defining force of the Second Age), but it is not the central narrative created by such heredity.<br /> <br /> I'd say the most basic narrative of a hereditary Exaltation is divided between &quot;Interesting family&quot; (on those occasions of people with good enough breeding that their nuclear and possibly extended family contains many Exalted) and &quot;Remarkable Ancestor (whose legacy informs what you're expected to live up to)&quot;, in those cases where you Exalt kind of inexplicably.<br /> <br /> The former particularly... I'd say there were Terrestrial families in the First Age who were no more nobility than, say, the Skywalker, Summers or Parr families are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T12:55:00-07:00","id":155112,"title":"","content":"Sidereals are absolutely behind most mortal nations in Creation!<br /> <br /> When that nation suddenly gets its act together and comes after me? It's not because I mooned the entire trade summit, it's because Sidereals.<br /> <br /> When those demon hunters know where I am? It's not because I'm dressed in enough gold to make Rameses II think I'm overdoing it, it's because Sidereals.<br /> <br /> When the hunters find their way out of that elaborate trap and come after me? It's not because they're actually pretty dangerous people, it's because Sidereals.<br /> <br /> When I can't find my keys and I limit break from dealing with the frustrating nature of Creation? It's because Sidereals hid them in my pocket.<br /> <br /> Some would say that there are only a hundred of those guys and they can't even begin to have the time to mess around with my vassals the honored Barons Pissant and Gadfly and even if they had that kind of time it'd be way easier to do so by working through the gods of my nation (which is actually something that kind of looks like their job), but<i> I know better</i>. SIDEREALS!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","user":"Guancyto","date":". 05-31-2014, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T13:18:41-07:00","id":155125,"title":"","content":"Hmm, now I'm considering the irony that would be present in the idea of turning the usual presentation or assumption on its head and say that the Scarlet Dynasty actually tends to have better breeding than even some of the more hardline Terrestrials of the First Age, and that alone can serve as a strong indication of just how far the world has fallen.<br /> <br /> What's a batter indication of a broken and diminished world; one in which your much-vaunted &quot;blood purity&quot; is not what it was a thousand years ago, or one in which international society and general technology level are so far down the drain that you've got to wring as much power as you can manage out of your bloodline in order to secure your position?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T13:24:43-07:00","id":155154,"title":"","content":"I told them, I told them, the Sidereals, you can't trust the Sidereals! They run up the flat to the back of the dragon and hold their tails so you can't fly no more and then you can't know your thoughts no more because they've already stolen the wrench to your mind! Mindbomb, the mindbomb! It's the only thing that will keep them out of your brain! It stops them coming through!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T13:35:20-07:00","id":155165,"title":"","content":"Mindbomb? That sounds COOL! I'm changing my answer to his!<br /> <br /> (That's two votes for mindbomb, we win!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","user":"Guancyto","date":". 06-02-2014, 01:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T13:39:15-07:00","id":155168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=153949#post153949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...what?<br /> <br /> That's completely off-base.<br /> <br /> The Wyld Hunt deals with the Anathema and existential threats such as the Fair Folk; they don't have anything to do with the Outcaste. Sure, Outcastes/Lost Eggs can get in trouble with the Realm, but dealing with them will never be a job for the Wyld Hunt - only for Dynasts or the Legions. And since there are more Outcastes than there are Dynasts, conducting a policy of systematically rooting out Lost Eggs that cause trouble would be a very poor idea indeed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if it's explicitly stated anywhere how many DBs exist outside of the influence of the Realm and Lookshy. Regardless, both of those states have a major interest in collecting as many DBs as they can, of the highest purity blood they can find, and can suffer a major setback if any Dragon-Blood decides to set up a cult to himself elsewhere (which goes against the Immaculate Philosophy, something most members of the Wyld Hunt won't take kindly to).<br /> <br /> Yes, any DB that can stay far enough away from the Immaculate Order or the Realm's forces can live well... provided he has the right kind of friends or a large enough bankroll (or lives far enough away) that people won't come by to try to recruit/capture/kill him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Furthermore, Outcastes thrive outside the Realm. The majority of nations or organization with influence have Outcastes in their employ, from Halta to the Haslanti League to the Lintha, with others working for the Guild or just becoming rulers in their own right. The Outcastes have incredible assets, and life is much, much easier from the get-go for them than it is for a mortal - those who want to strike out on their own might have a tough time doing so as would anyone, but the world at large prizes and desires their talents. </div> </div> </div>Right, and foremost among them are the two powers- the Realm and Lookshy- which are founded on the strength of their Dragon-Blooded rulers. Although if you have a bit more of a power base, you can probably expect a more... <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zy5K8ApSzhI\" target=\"_blank\">friendly approach.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;We do not quit playing because we grow old, we grow old because we quit playing.&quot; - Oliver Wendell Holmes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","name":"MrInsecure","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T13:49:30-07:00","id":155195,"title":"","content":"I don't know that the Realm/Lookshy is going to come down hard on a DB that sets up a power base independent of them, especially if it isn't in direct opposition to their goals. First of all the Realm doesn't really have the time or resources to go chasing after every lost egg (there are <i>tons</i> of them), and second, by setting themselves up as rulers, the Outcaste are directly reinforcing the whole culture of &quot;Divine Right of Dragons&quot; without the Realm even having to do anything at all.<br /> <br /> I also don't think that, should they have a problem with a particular Dragon-Blood, that capturing or killing them is the way to go. They're much more likely to use the carrot rather than the stick for the sole reason that coercing your prospective elemental demigods into joining your war machine tends to be a<i> terrible idea</i>. If you've got skills, the Realm wants them, surely. But so does everyone else. And if you want to rule a nation you had best be strong or rich or have powerful friends, but... that's <i>always</i> true when you want to rule a nation.<br /> <br /> Edit: Basically I think said friendly approach is the default mode, and if the Realm is trying to kill or kidnap an Outcaste for some reason other than conquering their lands, things have gone <i>very</i> wrong.<br /> <br /> Double edit: And it's not like they can't afford to play the long game. Sure, an Outcaste may be causing a lot of trouble <i>now</i>, but give them twenty years to start that biological clock ticking and set them wondering about legacy, and they'll see the merit in joining up with the greatest military force in history, right? Dinars flow like water and mortals (especially ones in the satrapies, who aren't even good Realm citizens) are never in short supply, but a powerful Dragon-Blooded officer is worth his weight in jade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","user":"Guancyto","date":". 05-31-2014, 05:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T14:05:33-07:00","id":155202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrInsecure</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=155168#post155168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if it's explicitly stated anywhere how many DBs exist outside of the influence of the Realm and Lookshy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not as a direct statement, no, but enough passing references are made to Outcastes just making their way in the world that one can derive a certain trend.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrInsecure</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless, both of those states have a major interest in collecting as many DBs as they can, <b>of the highest purity blood they can find</b></div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know, the only source that states or suggests that Found Eggs are intended for breeding purposes is the Second Edition write-up of House Tepet, which I think makes it suspect for several reasons.<br /> <br /> How high their blood purity is doesn't really matter, because they're for the legions and the Immaculate Order, not your children's bedchambers (or rather, they're not for marriage because being Outcaste means you already know that their bloodline is horribly mismanaged).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrInsecure</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">and can suffer a major setback if any Dragon-Blood decides to set up a cult to himself elsewhere</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would that be a major setback to the Realm? Heck, why is an Outcaste setting up a cult for themselves, as opposed to something else?<br /> <br /> Like, that seems like a less probable thing to do than setting themselves up as a ruler of a thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrInsecure</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">(which goes against the Immaculate Philosophy, something most members of the Wyld Hunt won't take kindly to).</div> </div> </div> </div>Is the Wyld Hunt going around destroying graven images as well?<br /> <br /> Not everything the Immaculate Philosophy opposes, or even opposes violently, warrents the Wyld Hunt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrInsecure</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, any DB that can stay far enough away from the Immaculate Order or the Realm's forces can live well... provided he has the right kind of friends or a large enough bankroll (or lives far enough away) that people won't come by to try to recruit/capture/kill him.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's really the general rubric of the Age of Sorrows, whether you're Exalted or not, isn't it?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T07:14:46-07:00","id":156470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrInsecure</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=155168#post155168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if it's explicitly stated anywhere how many DBs exist outside of the influence of the Realm and Lookshy.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Outcastes chapter in MOEP Dragon-Blooded suggests that there are probably as many Outcastes as there are Dynast Dragon-Blooded. Given how much smaller Lookshy is than the Realm, I'd suggest something in the region of eight to nine thousand. This is going by the oft-challenged figure of Ten Thousand Dragons, which MOEP Dragon-Blooded seems to take as literal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrInsecure</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=155168#post155168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless, both of those states have a major interest in collecting as many DBs as they can, of the highest purity blood they can find, and can suffer a major setback if any Dragon-Blood decides to set up a cult to himself elsewhere (which goes against the Immaculate Philosophy, something most members of the Wyld Hunt won't take kindly to).</div> </div> </div> </div>As a point of order, while the Realm is preoccupied by blood purity in those who would participate in its breeding programs, Lookshy is not. They care more about quantity than quality, so to speak. This is reflected by the punishing cost of the Breeding background for Lookshy characters.<br /> <br /> Moreover, while the Immaculate Philosophy is practiced in Lookshy, it is a muted, reformed variant that (at least until the 3e spoilers) lacks any official analogue of a Wyld Hunt. Lookshy culture stresses that religious beliefs should be personal and private, and dissent from the Philosophy is implied to be commonplace. That's not to say that a Lookshyan with a cult would be overlooked, but it's not like the Realm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=155202#post155202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the Wyld Hunt going around destroying graven images as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about the Wyld Hunt, but itinerant Immaculates are certainly doing that. Looking at you, Kassif.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T08:55:22-07:00","id":156562,"title":"","content":"The Wyld Hunt is not an evangelical institution, they're basically demon hunters. Whether the Lookshy Immaculates respect more private faith or not never should have really mattered to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T12:47:21-07:00","id":156833,"title":"","content":"No, but it might mean that the Lookshyan Shikari are more concerned with actual threats to Creation, humanity and Lookshy, not necessarily in that order, rather than religiously motivated persecution of Celestial Exalted. True, they would probably still go after Ma-Ha-Suchi or Rakshi, but that's because they are as much or even more of a monster than most demons (barring major character rewrites in 3e).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Aretii: &quot;As one of the players described it, 'After initiation, it was actually a relief seeing who had eyepatches or bandaged hands - you know what <i>they</i> sacrificed, instead of wondering what bits people cut out of their own souls to gain power.'&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/578-lord-sia","name":"Lord Sia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T16:40:02-07:00","id":157051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=154815#post154815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Zeniths are priest-king royalty, true... but the Dragon Blooded are still the nobility.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobility usually posesses one quality that is generally missing in Outcastes. It is <i>hereditary</i>. Remember, you need to have a large group of terrestrials before you can hope to get stable dragonblooded dynasties. Even if the founder/conqueror of a nation was a terrestrial, their children would likely fail to exalt. Thus, most stable families with power and influence in the world are purely mortal. There are several exceptions to this, of course. Third (after Realm and Looskhy) would be Cherak, but from what i remember, the &quot;genses&quot; of fourth such example (Port Calin) are already mostly mortal, due to lack of exalted numbers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T16:59:35-07:00","id":157083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=157051#post157051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobility usually posesses one quality that is generally missing in Outcastes. It is <i>hereditary</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Outcastes still get in on the &quot;nobility&quot; trope of the Dragon-Blooded, they just approach it from the &quot;forgotten scion of an ancient bloodline&quot; angle rather than receiving all the perks right from the start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T22:54:44-07:00","id":157546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=156562#post156562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Wyld Hunt is not an evangelical institution, they're basically demon hunters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. They're a militant\u200b institution, not an evangelical one. While there is some scope for an unofficial Wyld Hunt, it is very much (at least in 1e and 2e) the Order's game. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Sia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=156833#post156833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, but it might mean that the Lookshyan Shikari are more concerned with actual threats to Creation, humanity and Lookshy, not necessarily in that order, rather than religiously motivated persecution of Celestial Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Directions: Scavenger Lands</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">While the Solar Exalted are not hunted or shunned in Lookshy, their arrival is not considered good news. Peaceable Anathema have come to Lookshy and found cordial accommodations for the length of their visits, but their unpredictability combined with the raw power at their disposal makes them difficult to befriend.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly a witch hunt reception. Mind you, again, Lookshyan Wyld Hunts are mentioned in 3e spoilers, so this appears to be changing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=157051#post157051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobility usually posesses one quality that is generally missing in Outcastes. It is <i>hereditary</i>. Remember, you need to have a large group of terrestrials before you can hope to get stable dragonblooded dynasties. Even if the founder/conqueror of a nation was a terrestrial, their children would likely fail to exalt. Thus, most stable families with power and influence in the world are purely mortal. There are several exceptions to this, of course. Third (after Realm and Looskhy) would be Cherak, but from what i remember, the &quot;genses&quot; of fourth such example (Port Calin) are already mostly mortal, due to lack of exalted numbers.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a minor nitpick, Cherak is considered a part of the Realm, rather than an outcaste nation. <br /> <br /> Moreover, I see small Dragon-Blooded families and lesser dynasties being just as popular as lone bastards in those Outcastes that remain apart from the Realm. See the Fivefold Shades, Forest Witches and the Ollantijaya who I linked back on the first page. <br /> <br /> And I use the word bastards advisedly. Lone outcastes are nobility to the same extent as any unacknowledged noble bastard. I think the connection still holds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T01:11:59-07:00","id":157641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=157051#post157051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if the founder/conqueror of a nation was a terrestrial, their children would likely fail to exalt.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's my view that if you're Exalted, no matter how shoddy your bloodline is, you're entitled to one Exalted child. Usually the eldest, just to account for the possibility of accidents or only wanting one child. Certainly, I can't recall any reference to a Terrestrial who didn't have a single Exalted child.<br /> <br /> This <i>would</i> allow an Outcaste to maintain an extremely thin line of descent down from themselves, but it's usually not sustainable in the long run; all it takes is one death and the Exalting blood is cut off (although your mortal children will have descendents carrying the blood, amongst whom one will eventually Exalt).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T12:43:22-07:00","id":158113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=157641#post157641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's my view that if you're Exalted, no matter how shoddy your bloodline is, you're entitled to one Exalted child. Usually the eldest, just to account for the possibility of accidents or only wanting one child. Certainly, I can't recall any reference to a Terrestrial who didn't have a single Exalted child.<br /> <br /> This <i>would</i> allow an Outcaste to maintain an extremely thin line of descent down from themselves, but it's usually not sustainable in the long run; all it takes is one death and the Exalting blood is cut off (although your mortal children will have descendents carrying the blood, amongst whom one will eventually Exalt).</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. Going by the crunch alone, a child of a Terrestrial without Breeding and the average mortal has a 30% chance of Exalting. This chance is doubled for two Exalts having a child together. Normally I don't like rolling dice for such things, but this probability feels about right to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T12:48:49-07:00","id":158147,"title":"","content":"Thank you, Crumplepunch, for your plans to use Ollantijaya. The highest praise for a game writer is to be told one's work is useful.<br /> <br /> I imagine Creation has room for several more DB-led cultures, plus all the Outcastes who just do their own thing as individuals.<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T13:47:06-07:00","id":158228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=158113#post158113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going by the crunch alone, a child of a Terrestrial without Breeding and the average mortal has a 30% chance of Exalting. This chance is doubled for two Exalts having a child together. Normally I don't like rolling dice for such things, but this probability feels about right to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if those mechanics are taken purely in terms of an abstraction based on dramatic necessity rather than a literal depiction of the odds of children Exalting, I still don't quite like them for placing a higher probability of Exalted children in Outcastes of pitiful breeding than in unExalted Dynasts of exceptional breeding.<br /> <br /> Something just doesn't feel right in the idea that the mortal children of Mnemon and, say, V'Neef having worse odds of a child from their coupling inheriting Exaltation than some random Outcaste whose last Exalted ancestor was five hundred years ago and a random mortal of unknown stock. Not to mention how the Realm attitude towards Outcastes suggests that you actually get worse from a Dragon Blood with low Breeding than a well-bred mortal.<br /> <br /> I have high hopes for a Breeding Merit that will be extended to mortals.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T06:19:03-07:00","id":158964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=158228#post158228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if those mechanics are taken purely in terms of an abstraction based on dramatic necessity rather than a literal depiction of the odds of children Exalting, I still don't quite like them for placing a higher probability of Exalted children in Outcastes of pitiful breeding than in unExalted Dynasts of exceptional breeding.</div> </div> </div> </div>Preference of course, but I disagree. Outcastes are still Exalted, and mortals, however well bred, are not. The fix is easy enough though; allow mortal children of Exalts to use their parent's Breeding in the calculations of their own offspring. In the aforementioned case of the children of Mnemon (Breeding 5) and V'neef (Legendary Breeding), the chance of their children Exalting would be greater than an Exalted parent being involved, which I think is more than adequate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=158228#post158228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to mention how the Realm attitude towards Outcastes suggests that you actually get worse from a Dragon Blood with low Breeding than a well-bred mortal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah yes, because systems of hereditary government are so well known for their adherence to <i>sensible </i>traditions. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DShomshak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=158147#post158147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you, Crumplepunch, for your plans to use Ollantijaya. The highest praise for a game writer is to be told one's work is useful.<br /> I imagine Creation has room for several more DB-led cultures, plus all the Outcastes who just do their own thing as individuals.<br /> Dean Shomshak</div> </div> </div> </div>Well no, thank <i>you</i>. It was very good work and I wish there had been more chapters like it in the Directions. I enjoyed all of your Cleaning my Closet series but the Ollantijaya were the ones that I felt most inspired to create characters and stories for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 06-04-2014, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T08:49:14-07:00","id":159110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=158964#post158964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V'neef (Legendary Breeding),</div> </div> </div> </div>God I hate that Second Edition book so much. Hey, let's just diminish the nuanced political and economic climate behind the nomination of a new Great House and instead go with a ham-fisted idea of V'Neef having a kind of <i>super</i> breeding (that I suppose came from the Scarlet Empress engaging in an ancient magical org<i>fuckthstbooktohelll</i>)<br /> <br /> Ahem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Outcastes are still Exalted, and mortals, however well bred, are not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm personally not up on the idea that being Exalted necessarily says anything about your breeding, and thus your odds of producing Exalted descendants. Like, I get more interest, not to mention sense of consistency from the writing, that sometimes people of the most exceptional breeding don't Exalt (but that exceptional breeding still matters for producing people who are likely to), and sometimes people with the tiniest trickle of Dragon Blood from a thousand years ago do, lacking any of the necessary factors for creating a decent nuclear family, let alone a sustainable Dynasty. In this, I feel that the Exaltation is preserved as something numinous and working on mythic logic, rather than something one can optimize like the size of cattle.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo yes, I'd feel that if you're an Outcaste, you're kind of like an extremely distant cousin who, by nigh inscrutable chance, managed to be interesting enough to be considered a member of the family, and apart from the courtesy of one Exalted kid, the rest of that line has the same infinitesimally smaller chance of Exalting that the Outcaste did.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T12:04:38-07:00","id":159269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=157641#post157641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's my view that if you're Exalted, no matter how shoddy your bloodline is, you're entitled to one Exalted child. Usually the eldest, just to account for the possibility of accidents or only wanting one child. Certainly, I can't recall any reference to a Terrestrial who didn't have a single Exalted child.</div> </div> </div> </div>Logically, if every Dragon-Blood could always have at least one Exalted child no matter how thin the blood, the world would be overrun with them. You certainly wouldn't have mortal Realm patrician families; once your family marries enough unExalted Dynasts to produce the occasional Exalt, you have an Exalted bloodline that will never fade (barring unexpected disaster).<br /> <br /> Narratively, you lose the trope of, &quot;Alas for my people, as none of my children are fit to succeed me!&quot; And that would be a damned shame.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T12:08:26-07:00","id":159271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=157546#post157546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not exactly a witch hunt reception. Mind you, again, Lookshyan Wyld Hunts are mentioned in 3e spoilers, so this appears to be changing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your 2e quote is itself a departure from earlier material.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Seventh Legion interdicts the Realm's Wyld Hunt in the Scavenger Lands, for security reasons -- but this does not mean the Anathema are well-liked, or even tolerated, in Lookshy. The Legion dispatches units to destroy Anathema when it becomes aware of them but does not maintain any kind of proactive watch against them -- their missions are reactive in nature.&quot; (<b>Exalted: the Outcaste</b>, p. 23)<br /> <br /> (The text continues with a note that it's possible for a cautious Solar to establish peaceful contact with Lookshy, but that's not presented as the default the way it is in 2e.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T12:19:07-07:00","id":159282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=159271#post159271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your 2e quote is itself a departure from earlier material.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Seventh Legion interdicts the Realm's Wyld Hunt in the Scavenger Lands, for security reasons -- but this does not mean the Anathema are well-liked, or even tolerated, in Lookshy. The Legion dispatches units to destroy Anathema when it becomes aware of them but does not maintain any kind of proactive watch against them -- their missions are reactive in nature.&quot; (<b>Exalted: the Outcaste</b>, p. 23)<br /> <br /> (The text continues with a note that it's possible for a cautious Solar to establish peaceful contact with Lookshy, but that's not presented as the default the way it is in 2e.)</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds like a more reasonable approach. When I last used Lookshy in a game I took the middle road that Anathema are vilified but not actively hunted. Some sohei and other conservatives took the outspoken view that Lookshy should have its own Wyld Hunt to destroy the demons, while some progressive (and unscrupulous) officers wanted to court them for their own ends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T17:11:07-07:00","id":159456,"title":"","content":"Yeah, in 2nd ed Lookshy became, weirdly, a lot more comfortable with Anathema (and was kind of odd in lots of other ways too... I felt 2e Lookshy was in many ways poorly written, unless you take the whole thing as a propaganda piece about how wonderful Lookshy is).<br /> Yes, they're not the Realm. They're the glorious last remnant of a lost golden age society (at least, that's how they see it), the Shogunate. And in the Shogunate, Anathema were murdered wherever they were found.<br /> So, it's bizarre for Lookshy to be totally cool with Anathema. Of course, they severely lack the power or reach of the Realm, so it's not practical for them to go around hunting them, but that doesn't mean they like them. Their general experience with Anathema is, after all, working with the rest of the Scavenger Lands states to fight off giant invasions of barbarians and beastmen led by Lunars, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T20:31:01-07:00","id":159688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=159456#post159456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, in 2nd ed Lookshy became, weirdly, a lot more comfortable with Anathema (and was kind of odd in lots of other ways too... I felt 2e Lookshy was in many ways poorly written, unless you take the whole thing as a propaganda piece about how wonderful Lookshy is).<br /> Yes, they're not the Realm. They're the glorious last remnant of a lost golden age society (at least, that's how they see it), the Shogunate. And in the Shogunate, Anathema were murdered wherever they were found.<br /> So, it's bizarre for Lookshy to be totally cool with Anathema. Of course, they severely lack the power or reach of the Realm, so it's not practical for them to go around hunting them, but that doesn't mean they like them. Their general experience with Anathema is, after all, working with the rest of the Scavenger Lands states to fight off giant invasions of barbarians and beastmen led by Lunars, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assumed it was because centuries of alliance with the rest of the River Province including close ties with &quot;Hundred Gods Heresy 'R Us&quot; Great Forks had obliged Lookshy to take a more measured approach to things it would traditionally hate. Not to mention that Lookshy's heavy reliance on its failing arsenals and strong push towards creating and recreating wonders makes strategic bargaining with up and coming Solars highly desirable for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T22:11:07-07:00","id":159746,"title":"","content":"Well, that is somewhat true. I think that, as soldiers, they're practical enough to work alongside a Solar to defeat a Deathlord. Just because the Solar are body-snatching demons doesn't mean you should absolutely never team up with them to defeat a greater foe. Just don't expect them to invite the Solar round for tea afterwards.<br /> Certainly, you're right that they're used to teaming up with people who believe things that are opposed to their own beliefs. It's just that I think that an impression was given in 2nd ed, and I've heard this from some fans too, that they're totally cool with anathema, and that Solars can just go and hang out at Valkhawsen, which is very different and less believable than the 1st ed line that Minton quoted.<br /> <br /> Essentially, think of it as historical religions. They see them as religious enemies. 90% of the time, middle age Christians wouldn't ally with Muslims... but 10% of the time, screw the Byzantines, Muslims charge us less taxes. Or consider the 30 years war, where Catholic France allied with the Protestants because screw the Austrian Emperor, and Protestant Sweden allied with the Catholics because they wanted to conquer Denmark. The western Christian powers helped the Qing Dynasty crush the pseudo-Christian Taiping Heavenly Kingdom because it was dangerously socialist, and a corrupt Imperial monarchy is easier to exploit than a million fanatical peasants who believe they're ruled by Jesus Christ's younger brother. Or the way Christian Britain was allied with the Ottoman Muslims (until the slaughter of peasants in the Balkans got to much for them to ignore), because anti-Russian politics was considered more important than religion.<br /> And in the same way, Lookshy has teamed up many times with heathen god-worshippers and ghost-worshippers and so on to defeat their fellow Immaculates in the Realm (of course, that's reasonable because the enmity between different factions of the same religion can often eclipse what they feel about foreign religions, just because it's a more pressing problem, like the way Nestorian Christians used to fight for the Zorastrian Persians against Orthodox Christians in the Byzantine Empire, or for that matter the way today Sunni governments across the middle east receive American aid to combat Iran and it's Shi'ite or Alawite proxies like Hizb'allah and Bashir Assad).<br /> But that doesn't mean they're buddy-buddy with Anathema, they still dislike them, it's just that they haven't generally been as pressing an issue as, say, making sure everyone doesn't conquered by the Realm, or the Arzhecki, or recently Mask of Winters.<br /> <br /> Lookshy consider the Anathema evil, but they're the sorts of people who are willing to work with a lesser evil to defeat a greater evil.<br /> Whereas the Realm would never compromise (though that doesn't mean individual impious, ambitious DBs would never do so).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-05-2014, 01:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T22:14:55-07:00","id":159748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=159282#post159282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This sounds like a more reasonable approach. When I last used Lookshy in a game I took the middle road that Anathema are vilified but not actively hunted. Some sohei and other conservatives took the outspoken view that Lookshy should have its own Wyld Hunt to destroy the demons, while some progressive (and unscrupulous) officers wanted to court them for their own ends.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like a sensible approach to me. I'd do the same... but I disliked the portrayal of Lookshy in 2nd ed so much that I just had the whole city destroyed (as it's strongly hinted it was fated to be).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T22:20:13-07:00","id":159758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=158228#post158228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even if those mechanics are taken purely in terms of an abstraction based on dramatic necessity rather than a literal depiction of the odds of children Exalting, I still don't quite like them for placing a higher probability of Exalted children in Outcastes of pitiful breeding than in unExalted Dynasts of exceptional breeding.<br /> <br /> Something just doesn't feel right in the idea that the mortal children of Mnemon and, say, V'Neef having worse odds of a child from their coupling inheriting Exaltation than some random Outcaste whose last Exalted ancestor was five hundred years ago and a random mortal of unknown stock. Not to mention how the Realm attitude towards Outcastes suggests that you actually get worse from a Dragon Blood with low Breeding than a well-bred mortal.<br /> <br /> I have high hopes for a Breeding Merit that will be extended to mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it'd make a lot of sense for the first few hundred years of the 2nd age to have had loads of kingdoms run by noble DB families, who had been the regional Shogunate nobility, but whose kingdoms fell apart because they lose the purity.<br /> And also, for their to be some kingdoms today run by extremely in-bred DBs who have to marry their siblings to keep the blood pure, as its the only way to ensure the exaltation of their children.<br /> As happened in some historical dynasties, who believed their rulers were literal gods.<br /> <br /> On a slightly tangential note, have any of you guys ever had the players encounter non-Realm kingdoms run by DBs who trace their lineage back to the Shogunate? I've had a few. It just seems to make sense to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T23:52:16-07:00","id":159789,"title":"","content":"I've got a few of those. I also wrote up a whole tribal society who traced back to a Shogunate military unit, with essentially no dragonbloods left - drew a lot from battletech clans for ideas and mixed them with fantasy barbarians, basically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T00:08:23-07:00","id":159794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=159746#post159746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Certainly, you're right that they're used to teaming up with people who believe things that are opposed to their own beliefs. It's just that I think that an impression was given in 2nd ed, and I've heard this from some fans too, that they're totally cool with anathema, and that Solars can just go and hang out at Valkhawsen, which is very different and less believable than the 1st ed line that Minton quoted.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, aside from the short passage I quoted there is little suggestion in 2e that Lookshy are anathema-bros.<br /> <br /> Speaking of the Valkshawken, for example, while the White Treatise mentions that it is rumoured that Solar students attend there, they are disguised as god-blooded metics. They only get away with it because of the influence of the director Amilar Kraik, a crazy bastard who hopes to use any means at his disposal to forestall his degenerative curse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T04:52:52-07:00","id":159903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=158964#post158964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mnemon (Breeding 5) and V'neef (Legendary Breeding)</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure Scroll of Heroes bumped Little Red to Legendary Breeding (which didn't exist for her Aspect Book write up).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T05:47:35-07:00","id":159926,"title":"","content":"Scroll of Exalts actually did the bumping. SoH was just an enabler there. <br /> <br /> Of course, the merit is really just an attepmpt at reintroducing the legendary background from Dreams of the First Age to the modern era, which possibly makes it an even worse idea depending on your opinion of that particular book. It's supposed to represent a dragonblood with no mortal ancestors at all (or at least none since the exaltation of the original 10000), which is a role it may have usurped from breeding 5 but there you go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T06:07:30-07:00","id":159939,"title":"","content":"As far as I am concerned, Legendary Breeding is no worse than the Breeding background in general. It's just Breeding 6 in all but name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T16:25:58-07:00","id":161245,"title":"","content":"The Linowan kingdom had a DB founder whose lineage died out. I don't remember offhand if that detail was mentioned in Kingdom of Halta or whether the author of the CoTD: East chapter's author and I slipped that in.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, for the OP: If it hasn't been mentioned yet, the Compass of Terrestrial Direction books describe several Outcaste DB characters.<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T17:24:48-07:00","id":161284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DShomshak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=161245#post161245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Linowan kingdom had a DB founder whose lineage died out. I don't remember offhand if that detail was mentioned in Kingdom of Halta or whether the author of the CoTD: East chapter's author and I slipped that in.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, for the OP: If it hasn't been mentioned yet, the Compass of Terrestrial Direction books describe several Outcaste DB characters.<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak</div> </div> </div> </div>Shame the line died out, would have rather has it diluted, to later emerge many many years later, with it's own trappings and legends, rather than the true origin, History skewed by myth and legend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T23:38:41-07:00","id":161451,"title":"","content":"Huh, I didn't notice that about the Linowan, that's pretty cool.<br /> You could do a Linowan Outcaste character claiming that being a DB proves they're descended from the founder (which it may or may not) and thus they should become King of the Linowan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T01:35:17-07:00","id":161491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=161284#post161284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shame the line died out, would have rather has it diluted, to later emerge many many years later, with it's own trappings and legends, rather than the true origin, History skewed by myth and legend.</div> </div> </div> </div>All it takes is one bastard history didn't account for, so it's totally plausible. Terrestrial bloodlines do resurface like that from time to time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T02:25:19-07:00","id":161510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrInsecure</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=153917#post153917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, in terms of non-Realm DBs, they basically split into two groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nooooooooo. oo. Nonononono. A thousand times no.<br /> <br /> First, your description is, I think, slightly too Realm-centric -- the Realm is absolutely the most powerful nation in the world, but it's like, say, America, or Rome; powers exist outside of it, even ones so far away that it's almost a distant story (if a very <i>big</i> story.) There are groups of Dragon-Blooded even in those distant realms. The Realm defines all outcastes according to a doctrine that says that it is the sole representative of all DBs everywhere, but even with its vast power it isn't remotely close to being able to actually enforce that doctrine creationwide. What you describe is definitely the case on the Blessed Isle itself, and to some extent or another it's felt throughout the Threshold, as well as several other places where the Realm can project direct and immediate power; but that doesn't cover all of Creation by a long shot, and there are still Dragon-Blooded everywhere else, too.<br /> <br /> I think the books have also sometimes oversold the ability of the Realm to attract Lost Eggs, and the extent to which the Realm is capable of actually defining the experience of being an Outcaste outside its borders -- yes, some DBs will take them up on it; if you Exalt as a Lost Egg in an area controlled by the Realm, you'll feel a lot of pressure. But it's a mistake to assume that the Realm simply wants to attract as many DBs as possible. A small number of people with no family trickling in is good; a huge migration of established DB families with their own resources and connections is bad, because it threatens the Realm's current order. Which isn't to say that they overtly discourage anyone -- official Realm policy is that it stands for all DBs everywhere -- but when you really look at it, the coin and the razor is a pretty ugly (in some cases, almost insulting) choice to offer a Prince of the Earth, isn't it? This is not an accident. They want the DBs who are in a position to be forced into that choice (in other words, the ones who can be used).<br /> <br /> (It is important to realize, basically, that most DBs outside the Realm and certain parts of the Threshold aren't going to think of themselves as &quot;Lost Eggs&quot; or even &quot;outcastes&quot; at all; they'll just think of themselves as <i>Dragon-Blooded</i>.)<br /> <br /> But if you're slightly overestimating the impact of the Realm, you're <i>vastly</i> overestimating Lookshy. Lookshy is perhaps the largest concentration of DBs outside the Realm, but I seriously doubt it was originally intended to hold that honor by a particularly overwhelming margin. If the entire Blessed Isle were to drop into a bottomless pit tomorrow, Lookshy would be just one of countless squabbling groups of DBs trying to step into the void.<br /> <br /> I think that part of the problem was that Lookshy was written up as an example of how DB societies exist outside the auspices of the Realm; and then proceeded to be used as the go-to &quot;other DBs&quot; and &quot;alternate axis of power&quot; example forever, until Creation shrunk to the point where you had the Realm and Lookshy sticking up out of a cartoonishly tiny world lobbing Soul-Breaker Orbs at each other, and nothing else of note -- like <a href=\"http://www.photoguides.net/wp-content/uploads/2010/01/Snowy_night___Tiny_Planet_v1_by_vxside.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>, but with a not-round world.<br /> <br /> Another part of the problem is that the outcaste book dedicated a bunch of text to Lookshy, and then a bunch of text (as the other major example of a DB organization outside the Realm) to... the Forest Witches. Who are totally cool and all, but were so weird that nobody really knew what to do with them.<br /> <br /> Anyway, as a general rule, the key things to remember about DBs are, almost uniquely among Creation's Exalted, that they have had time to produce generations worth of established, existing legitimacy almost anywhere, and are able to pass their power down through blood to maintain direction and political power across those generations. That means that it is <i>very</i> easy to see a DB family, or some consortiums of DB families, rising to prominence all over the world, especially in areas where they face less direct opposition from rival clans or other Exalted. I don't think that every DB is guaranteed to produce DB heirs, but still -- all it takes is one DB with a bit of luck to establish a small, local dynasty, so I expect it's happened all over the place. These local dynasties are a lot more transient than the Realm (all it would take is a bit of bad luck for a generation to wipe your typical one out, say, and many could be extinguished in short order by a dedicated, skilled, and lucky assassin), but they're still capable of significantly shaping many parts of the setting.<br /> <br /> (I think another part of the reason why these have tended to be downplayed is because the Realm itself likely downplays them. This vision of &quot;you are either a member of the Realm or you're some random nobody who Exalted to mortal parents&quot; very much suits the Realm's leading families; but I doubt it actually reflects reality, especially in places that are comparatively far outside of the Realm's reach.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 06-08-2014, 08:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T03:42:51-07:00","id":161547,"title":"","content":"I'll admit, the idea that even the lowest bred Terrestrial can have a single Exalted child is a bit of a concession to my expectation that there'd be a sizable number of people who'd find it objectionable to say they can have Dragon Blooded characters who can never have such children. That and just following through the logic<br /> <br /> Still, I wonder about some stuff...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=159269#post159269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Logically, if every Dragon-Blood could always have at least one Exalted child no matter how thin the blood, the world would be overrun with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>This I don't follow at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You certainly wouldn't have mortal Realm patrician families; once your family marries enough unExalted Dynasts to produce the occasional Exalt, you have an Exalted bloodline that will never fade (barring unexpected disaster).</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't most patricians get hardly any access to unExalted Dynasts at all? I mean, the patricians are supposed to vastly outnumber the Scarlet Dynasty anyway, aren't they, there's not even enough mortals scions of the Exalted to marry off into a fraction of them, and the majority of those are being married to one another before they're married to a patrician. Plus, isn't it generally the case that somebody who Exalts from the patricians is immediately snatched up by a Great House, and thus becomes irrelevant to patrician breeding at all?<br /> <br /> There might be a few dozen patrician families with a thin, but sustainable, line of Dragon Blooded running though them, which if we're to bring back the idea of the Realm having minor Houses (which Lea so desperately wants) is a good thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Narratively, you lose the trope of, &quot;Alas for my people, as none of my children are fit to succeed me!&quot; And that would be a damned shame.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a narrative I find particularly compelling enough to find it such a shame, and even then I find myself picturing scenarios where a person puts all their hopes and pressures on the one child who manages to Exalt and thus crushes them, or the one Exalted child has none of the personality or aptitude or inclination to be good at the same thing and so views the power as going to waste (or conversely, they're excited about the child who does show such inclinations, who then fails to Exalt).<br /> <br /> Succession crisis in general feels like a poor fit for any of the Exalted, barring the highly unusual circumstances of the Scarlet Empress.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T06:38:35-07:00","id":161621,"title":"","content":"The five shades association is a organization of DB that do not belong to either the Realm or Lookshy &amp; have a pretty strong power base as they have opposed the realm &amp; everyone that tries to take away their power or encroach on their turf. They are described as being a cross between the 5 hidden villages from the anime naruto &amp; the mafia and are probably part of or rivals of the guild that part was never specified or maybe it was &amp; i overlooked that part. Regardless their are other groups of DB besides the Realm &amp; Lookshy out there. They are in the Scroll of the monk book. I plan on using them in my current game as a rival to the guild &amp; the realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you think nobody cares if you're alive, try missing a couple of payments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2890-walker-of-ebony-clouds","name":"Walker-of-Ebony-Clouds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T06:48:58-07:00","id":161648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=159903#post159903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Little Red</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's the cutest thing I've ever heard anyone call Mnemon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T08:24:56-07:00","id":161726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=161547#post161547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll admit, the idea that even the lowest bred Terrestrial can have a single Exalted child is a bit of a concession to my expectation that there'd be a sizable number of people who'd find it objectionable to say they can have Dragon Blooded characters who can never have such children.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're playing a heroic mortals game in which the players all want their characters to Exalt, I'm sure you'd find it objectionable to say that your mortal characters can never Exalt. Such an event would be orders of magnitude less likely than a given Lost Egg's children Exalting. And yet, somehow it will happen!<br /> <br /> PCs tend to be exceptional, and much can be accomplished by talking to your Storyteller. This is not news.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=161547#post161547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That and just following through the logic</div> </div> </div> </div>What logic?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T08:40:31-07:00","id":161756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=161726#post161726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">PCs tend to be exceptional, and much can be accomplished by talking to your Storyteller. This is not news.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an aside, I agree with this. My main problem is that for people who try to reverse engineer mechanical statements into setting assumptions, and to a certain degree we all do, it would be helpful to have a sidebar directly stating &quot;What is good for one game, and one exceptional character is not good as a statement for the gameline as a whole&quot; somewhere in the corebook, preferably in the storytelling chapter. It seems to be a major point of contention; and constantly comes up in arguments about the Reclamation, Lost Eggs, Deathlords winning, etc etc etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T12:00:43-07:00","id":161897,"title":"","content":"As an aside on the Linowan Nation Dragon-Blooded, in our group's head-canon there's upwards of 500 Exalts in multiple thriving, healthy bloodlines across the boat clans with a great deal of them part of the royal clan (or married into it). Their existence balances out the enormous supernatural advantages Halta is favored with (sentient animals, targeted magic diseases, gossamer weapons, fae raid leaders, etc) and adds to the diversity of &quot;outcaste&quot; groups across Creation.<br /> <br /> There should be dozens of Cheraks, Five Shades mafia/tongs and mini-Lookshy fiefs all over the place, with thousands of Hill-Crushing Heroes in every direction wandering around doing whatever outcastes feel like doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T19:20:49-07:00","id":166451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=161648#post161648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's the cutest thing I've ever heard anyone call Mnemon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll have to remember it for my Dawn to use.<br /> <br /> Since that shard's version of Mnemon is the party's sorcerous support, having given up her Pride as sacrifice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T20:59:43-07:00","id":167520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/153881-independent-dragon-blooded?p=154415#post154415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always found it disappointing that as good as the Aspect books of 1E were, they only covered Realm Dragonbloods. I want to hear about Lost Eggs, or Outcasts. I want bloodlines of Dragonblooded significant to cultures, nations, or even religions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in 1e the idea of outcastes was pretty raw actually, so much so that the Dragon-blooded book was chock-full of stuff about the Realm as a whole and we only got a look at the lost Eggs as more than an afterthought in a module of their own that came much later (one year after all main exalts in fact).<br /> <br /> Actually, there were a few in the last two castebooks, Ranya Petris, a water-aspected Gethamane turned airboat captain, Odessa, the possibly the last queen of an island kingdom devastated by beastmen pirates and adopted into the House V'neef decades ago and Teresu Gido (that gets mentioned in MoEP: DB and statted in Scroll of Exalts), while Aspectbook: Wood gives us Rutanjali, the Queen of the Wood, a young village girl turned by the twists of her life and fate into bride of a King of Wood and queen &amp; general of his elemental court and armies, closer to spirits of the forest than the mortals of her past and probably my favorite outcaste concept ever. Ranya and Rutanjali in particular are among the narrators of their respective castebooks, making up 2/25 of the aspectbooks narrative.<br /> <br /> Speaking of outcaste NPCs - Bastions of the North has a haslanti admiral i think and Kingdom of Halta offers us Mors Ialden, the ex-lieutenant of the Bull of the North, a wood-aspected icewalker chief that, if circunstances were a little different, who knows, he might have been the Bull of the North instead of Yurgen Kaneko. And if memory tricks me not one of the Guild factors in Manacle &amp; Coin was a Lookshy native.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-13-2014, 12:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}